1
00:00:02,065 --> 00:00:06,665
Archivist — engineering intelligence, mapped.

2
00:00:06,965 --> 00:00:12,565
Ask your codebase anything. Every answer arrives wired to the code that proves it.

3
00:00:15,828 --> 00:00:23,128
A living graph of the codebase — read live from FalkorDB.

4
00:00:23,428 --> 00:00:29,828
Hubs and fan-in — every number read from the graph, never estimated.

5
00:00:31,751 --> 00:00:38,151
Search jumps straight into the call graph.

6
00:00:41,139 --> 00:00:47,739
Selection lights the neighbourhood — the inspector carries the facts.

7
00:00:51,110 --> 00:00:58,610
Paths light up hop by hop — weak, resolver-guessed edges are flagged, never hidden.

8
00:01:03,211 --> 00:01:09,511
Ask anything — the agent answers from the graph, one ribbon per step.

9
00:01:09,811 --> 00:01:19,811
Every step keeps its tools, its rows, and the exact Cypher that fetched them.

10
00:01:22,978 --> 00:01:32,278
Click a step — its evidence lights the canvas, live.

11
00:01:36,684 --> 00:01:46,284
History steps replay as a commit → file chain.

12
00:01:48,183 --> 00:01:53,783
It remembers across sessions.

13
00:01:54,083 --> 00:01:59,683
Investigations become episodes; findings become bi-temporal facts.

14
00:01:59,983 --> 00:02:08,583
Superseded versions stay in memory — invalidated, never deleted.

15
00:02:10,384 --> 00:02:15,584
FalkorDB is the context layer — not a bolt-on. One graph per repo.

16
00:02:16,588 --> 00:02:25,388
Architecture, the three tracks, and honest limits — for judges and the curious.

